Ultracopier integration for Dolphin's Ctrl+V (catchcopy v0002 + fallback).

TARGET VERSION: Dolphin 26.04.x (KF6 / Qt6). The API this patch relies on --
KUrlMimeData::urlsFromMimeData(), KIO::paste(), KIO::PasteJob::itemCreated,
KJobWidgets::setWindow(), DolphinView::slotItemCreated/slotPasteJobResult and the members
m_clearSelectionBeforeSelectingNewItems / m_markFirstNewlySelectedItemAsCurrent -- is pinned in
plugins/CopyEngine/Ultracopier-Spec/test/fmshim/dolphin_api_stub.h, and the patched pasteToUrl()
below is extracted from THIS file and executed against a real Ultracopier by
plugins/CopyEngine/Ultracopier-Spec/test/cases/dolphin_paste_patch.py. If a newer Dolphin renames
any of those, that case stops building -- which is the signal to refresh this patch.

Behaviour: Ctrl+V is offered to Ultracopier over the catchcopy socket; if Ultracopier REFUSES the
order (reply code 5004 -- e.g. an sftp:// url on a build without KIO) Dolphin does the paste with
its own KIO copier, so a paste is never lost. A cut's clipboard is cleared only once the order was
accepted. (`patch` ignores this text: it starts reading at the first "diff --git" line.)

